  {
    "id": "comment-architecture",
    "type": "comment",
    "name": "Pineapple Hub — MQTT Architecture",
    "info": "ESP32 Firmware publishes to:\n  pineapple/scale1/availability  (retained, QoS 1) — \"online\" | \"offline\"\n  pineapple/scale1/data          (QoS 1) — { weight_g, grade, status, ts }\n  pineapple/scale1/device_state  (QoS 1) — button/LCD/system state\n\nReact App subscribes to:\n  pineapple/scale1/#             (wildcard — all scale telemetry)\n  pineapple/vision/zone1         — \"occupied\" | \"clear\"\n  pineapple/vision/zone2         — \"occupied\" | \"clear\"\n  pineapple/hmi/+/state          — switch state wildcard\n\nReact App publishes to:\n  pineapple/hmi/{switchId}/set   — switch commands → echoed below\n\nAll flows connect to Aedes broker (node-red/broker.js):\n  TCP  : 0.0.0.0:1884  ← ESP32 + Node-RED\n  WS   : 0.0.0.0:9001  ← React app",
    "x": 180,
    "y": 20,
    "wires": []
  },
  {
    "id": "comment-seed-data",
    "type": "comment",
    "name": "━━━ DEV MODE: Seed Data Generator ━━━",
    "info": "DISABLE THESE NODES (double-click → Enabled: false) when the real ESP32\nis connected. Otherwise seed data conflicts with real firmware data.\n\nGenerates realistic crate weights (12–16 kg) every 2 seconds for testing\nthe web app dashboard without physical hardware.",
    "x": 180,
    "y": 120,
    "wires": []
  },
